{
  "tema": 6231,
  "slug": "gustar-atraccion",
  "titulo": "Using gustar to express personal attraction",
  "subtitulo": "Me gustas. ¿Le gusto? Se gustan.",
  "foto": "t08.jpg",
  "regla": "To say you like someone romantically, the person who is liked is the subject: Tú me gustas = I like you (lit. you are pleasing to me). Gustar is conjugated for that person: gusto, gustas, gusta, gustamos, gustan.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Gustar** can mean being **attracted** to someone. The person who **is liked** is the **subject**, and the verb agrees with them. The person who **does the liking** is the indirect pronoun."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Subject",
            "gustar"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "gusto"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "gustas"
            ],
            [
              "él, ella, usted",
              "gusta"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros",
              "gustamos"
            ],
            [
              "ustedes, ellos",
              "gustan"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Literally: **Tú me gustas** = _You are pleasing to me_ = **I like you**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "You can drop the subject (**yo, tú**) and the **a mí, a ti** part, but never the short pronoun (**me, te, le...**)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: flip the English. _I like you_ → you please me → **me gustas**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "(Yo) ==te gusto== (a ti).",
              "en": "You like me. (I'm pleasing to you.)"
            },
            {
              "es": "==Me gustas==.",
              "en": "I like you."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Le gusto==.",
              "en": "He / she likes me."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Le gustas==.",
              "en": "He / she likes you."
            },
            {
              "es": "Ella ==le gusta==.",
              "en": "He / she likes her."
            },
            {
              "es": "Ellos ==le gustan==.",
              "en": "He / she likes them."
            },
            {
              "es": "Nosotros ==te gustamos==, ¿verdad?",
              "en": "You like us, right?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Ustedes ==me gustan== mucho.",
              "en": "I really like you guys."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "reciproco",
      "titulo": "Liking each other",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "When the liking goes both ways, use **nos** or **se**:"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Nosotras ==nos gustamos== mucho.",
              "en": "We like each other a lot."
            },
            {
              "es": "Ellos ==se gustan==, se nota.",
              "en": "They like each other, you can tell."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Yo gusto a ti."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Me gustas."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "_I like you_: **tú** is the subject."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Me gusta tú."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Me gustas tú."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "The verb agrees with **tú**."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "¿Gusto a ti?"
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "¿Te gusto?"
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Keep the short pronoun."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
